Allow tagged PPPoE over the QCA4B persistent virtual port.

The QCA4B data path already maps the WAN user port to a persistent VP and
the PPE PPPoE session table matches the session ID and peer address on that
VP. Requiring a physical-port VLAN VSI for the same session rejects every
tagged PPPoE flow on RE-CS-06 before any hardware flow is installed.

Keep the VLAN VSI requirement for physical underlays, but let a QCA4B VP
carry tagged PPPoE directly.

--- a/target/linux/qualcommbe/patches-6.18/0652-net-ethernet-qualcomm-ppe-manage-dsa-pppoe-flow-lifecycle.patch
+++ b/target/linux/qualcommbe/patches-6.18/0652-net-ethernet-qualcomm-ppe-manage-dsa-pppoe-flow-lifecycle.patch
@@ -604,16 +604,18 @@
 +	 * The caller already holds its flow's VP reference.
 +	 */
 +	if (vp >= 0) {
-+		/* VLAN-over-VP needs VP translation rules, not a physical rule. */
-+		if (session->svid >= 0 || session->cvid >= 0)
-+			return -EOPNOTSUPP;
++		/* QCA4B already owns the user-port identity in the VP. The
++		 * PPPoE session table matches SID and peer on that VP, so a
++		 * tagged underlay must not allocate a physical-port VSI.
++		 */
 +		ret = ppe_vp_ref_qca4b(ft->ppe_dev, vp, session->port);
 +		if (ret)
 +			return ret;
  	}
  
 -	return -ENOENT;
-+	if (session->svid >= 0 || session->cvid >= 0) {
++	/* A physical underlay still needs a VLAN VSI for tagged PPPoE. */
++	if (vp < 0 && (session->svid >= 0 || session->cvid >= 0)) {
 +		vlan = ppe_ft_vlan_get(ft, session->port, session->svid,
 +				       session->cvid, session->vlan_mtu,
 +				       session->keep_svid,
